\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}},\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}})=\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}})=\\frac{4z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{4z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}+\\frac{16{z}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{17({x}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$\\,$ $\\sqrt{17}\\,$ and $\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429097 #edb/ref 1030 0.3333333333333333 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429097 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.333333; nearest selected fraction = 1/3. Crossing activity numbers [3]; waits [3]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1/3 (1/3). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/multivariable-frequency-estimates.json, pair 3602->1790. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relations